    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The problem involves the sum of consecutive powers of 3, generated starting from \\(3^0\\) and adding the next higher power in the sequence.\n\nThe sequence is as follows:\n- The first term is \\(3^0\\).\n- The second term is \\(3^0 + 3^1\\).\n- The third term is \\(3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2\\).\n- The fourth term is \\(3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3\\).\n\nWe need to find the simplified value of the fourth term, \\(3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3\\).\n\nLet's break down the steps:\n1. Calculate each power of 3.\n2. Sum the powers of 3 from \\(3^0\\) to \\(3^3\\).\n\nWe'll perform these calculations using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate each power of 3\npowers_of_3 = [3**i for i in range(4)]\n\n# Sum the powers of 3 from 3^0 to 3^3\nsum_of_powers = sum(powers_of_3)\nprint(sum_of_powers)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe simplified value of the fourth term in the sequence is \\(\\boxed{40}\\).",
