    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The given sequence is a combination of consecutive powers of 3, starting with $3^0$, $3^0 + 3^1$, $3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2$, and so on. The fourth term in this sequence can be written as:\n\n\\[\n3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3\n\\]\n\nTo find the value of this expression, we calculate each power of 3 individually and then sum them up.\n\nFirst, we calculate each term:\n\\[\n3^0 = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n3^1 = 3\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 = 9\n\\]\n\\[\n3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nNext, we sum these values:\n\\[\n3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3 = 1 + 3 + 9 + 27\n\\]\n\nWe perform the addition step-by-step:\n\\[\n1 + 3 = 4\n\\]\n\\[\n4 + 9 = 13\n\\]\n\\[\n13 + 27 = 40\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the fourth term in the sequence is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{40}\n\\]",
